  "previous_goal_turn_classification": "Progress: committed verified SQLite snapshot and MySQL reconciliation components, recorded their proof, and confirmed the Starmap #189 merge.",
  "changes": [
    "Portable, private SQLite images now export all thirteen known logical tables from a consistent SQLite, PostgreSQL, or MySQL snapshot. Export rejects unknown tables, columns, triggers, row-security tables, pending MySQL attempts, and incomplete migration sets.",
    "Import verifies the image before copying into an empty, migrated target. Migration ownership and native transaction locks serialize competing imports. The required callback restricts restored authority in the same transaction. Failure rolls back the records.",
    "Migration 0012 retains reconciliation evidence on every backend and preserves PostgreSQL microseconds in MySQL timestamp columns. Finer timestamp precision refuses network SQL import.",
    "Transfers preserve audit allocation floors, including deleted IDs. PostgreSQL uses transactional sequence restart. MySQL allocation gaps survive a rollback without resetting the retained floor.",
    "Scoped MySQL settings enforce UTC timestamp conversion, strict data conversion, and fresh allocator metadata. Cleanup restores prior session settings after success and failure."
  ],
