  "candidate_failures": [
    "The first PostgreSQL-to-MySQL transfer refused native microsecond migration timestamps because MySQL used TIMESTAMP without fractional precision. Migration 0012 and new table declarations now preserve six digits.",
    "The exhausted-counter test found MySQL clamping AUTO_INCREMENT to MaxInt64 after consuming and deleting that ID. Subtracting one underreported the retained allocation floor. A second real test demonstrated reuse of the deleted final ID.",
    "Import now refuses an exhausted signed audit counter on MySQL before copying records. SQLite and PostgreSQL retain exhausted counters and reject later automatic IDs. This is a documented representation limit, not a claimed MySQL success."
  ],
